// An extern struct's CONSTRUCTOR argument is a bind position (it was the aggregate initializer until KR-53,
// which judged nothing): this exact
// program was accepted while the same bind written `d.f = wrong;` was refused (tests/fnptr_basic's
// sibling rule). A shape-mismatched function reaching a function pointer is the UB class the bind funnel
// exists to prevent — the indirect call then passes the wrong number of arguments, which UBSan's
// `function` check would catch and which is disabled suite-wide for an unrelated reason. Its twin is
// tests/xfail/foreign_entry_via_extern_agg, the same leak costing a THREADING guarantee.
fnptr int32 Op(int32 x);

@generate(of)
type extern value Desc { public Op f; public int32 n; }

fn int32 wrong(int32 a, int32 b) { return a + b; }   // two params, not one

fn int32 main() {
    Desc d = Desc.of(f: wrong, n: 1);   // ERROR: `wrong` does not match `Op`
    return d.n;
}
